  "title": "Advancements in Active Learning for Object Detection through Generative Verification",
  "summary": "Active learning reduces the cost of annotating data while improving detection accuracy through a new signal-based approach that leverages generative verification. This method outperforms existing criteria and provides a more reliable and cost-effective solution.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "A supervised contrastive term added to the training objective shapes a per-object embedding space where distance encodes class membership.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The criterion requires no ensemble, auxiliary predictor, or repeated inference, and its entire cost is 2.89M parameters, an increase of 8.3% over a bare detector.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "It beats the posterior of the same detector in every round when a selection is made, by up to 1.08% mAP50 against run to run deviations of 0.02% to 0.18%.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The signal outperforms output-uncertainty, feature-geometry, perturbation, and ensemble criteria, gaining about one mAP50 point per round on MS-COCO.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
